{
  "_note": "Style category per token, from the Categories frame of the Open Source Dynamic Fonts Figma file. Figma organises on TWO axes at once and names them into one string: a style (Clean Sans Serif, More Character Sans Serif, Serif, Decorative) and a case (a \"Caps\" prefix or not). Only the style is recorded here. Case is NOT taken from Figma — it is read from each family's own cuts in library3.js, which is what actually shipped and disagreed with Figma on five families. \"Unassigned — no caps sibling\" is not a style: it is Figma noting a missing caps sibling, and 23 of its 25 members are roman-only. Those tokens get style \"Unassigned\", meaning no style was assigned. Kept out of library3.js because that file is generated by _build/make_library3.js.",
